Subject: [PATCH 0/3] notmuch: Tag superseded series and hide them
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:15:26 +0000

Old versions of a series stay on the list next to the current one,
and a reader has to open each thread to tell which is live. This
series derives a superseded tag from the list itself, as decided in
"Re: Supporting status trailers in emails" [1], and hides the tagged
threads from searches.

Patch 1 tags the thread a revised cover letter names on its "Link to
vN: id:<message-id>" line. Run over the list as it stands, it tags 24
threads, one per Link line.

Patch 2 tags the thread of any message whose closing trailers include
Superseded-by, found with git interpret-trailers. A quoted trailer does
not count. It is for the series no Link line covers, such as one a
different series replaces. Any sender may write it, and the hook needs
git.

Patch 3 adds superseded to search.exclude_tags in the sample config.
Only new installs get it; an existing ~/.notmuch-config needs the tag
added by hand. One effect to weigh: where it is excluded, inbox mail
in a superseded thread drops out of tag:inbox searches too. claude's
config does not exclude it, so lab-process-mail still answers such
mail.

Approved and rejected are left out until their form is settled; the
open question is in the same thread [2].

The series needs "[PATCH] notmuch: Tag patches reported committed"
[3], which is not yet applied. It reworks the same tagging batch in
mail-tag.sh, and its patch id is in the prerequisite-patch-id line
below.

I tested each patch against a scratch notmuch database built from a
copy of the maildir, with four added replies: a closing trailer, one
above a signature, a quoted one, and one followed by more text. The
first two tag their threads and the others do not.

